<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>6.3.5: Using the Factor Theorem</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01623</md:content-id>
    <md:title>6.3.5: Using the Factor Theorem</md:title>
    <md:uuid>5a75d066-60bf-48a9-b03d-b7c239a71c3e</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section class="practice" id="sect-00001"><title>Cool Down</title>
<para id="para-00001">In all the division problems we completed that had a remainder of zero, we say that the divisor was a factor of the dividend.</para>
<para id="para-00002">Whenever a divisor, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mi>c</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, divides a polynomial function, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>, and results in a remainder of zero, we say <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mi>c</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is a factor of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
<para id="para-00003">This leads us to the Factor Theorem.</para>

<note id="note-00001">
  <title>FACTOR THEOREM</title>
  
  <para id="para-00005">For any polynomial function <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>,</para>
  <list id="list-00001">
    <item>if <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mi>c</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is a factor of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>, then <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>c</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</item>
    <item>if <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>c</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, then <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mi>c</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is a factor of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</item>
  </list>
</note>

<para id="para-00006">Use the Factor Theorem to determine whether the binomial is a factor of the given polynomial function. Be prepared to show your reasoning.</para>

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise id="exer-00001">
  <problem id="prob-00001">
    <para id="para-00007">Is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> a factor of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>125</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
    </problem><solution id="sol-00001">
    
    
  
  <para id="para-00008">Compare your answer:</para>
    
    <para id="para-00009">Yes, because <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>125</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>125</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>125</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
  
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise id="exer-00002">
  <problem id="prob-00002">
    <para id="para-00010">Is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> a factor of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>216</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
    </problem><solution id="sol-00002">
    
    
  
  <para id="para-00011">Compare your answer:</para>
    
    <para id="para-00012">Yes, because <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>216</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>216</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>216</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
  
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise id="exer-00003">
  <problem id="prob-00003">
    <para id="para-00013">Is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> a factor of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>21</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>18</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
    </problem><solution id="sol-00003">
    
    
  
  <para id="para-00014">Compare your answer:</para>
    
    <para id="para-00015">Yes, because <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>21</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>18</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>27</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>72</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>63</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>18</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
  
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise id="exer-00004">
  <problem id="prob-00004">
    <para id="para-00016">Is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> a factor of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>14</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>?
    </para>
    </problem><solution id="sol-00004">
    
    
  
  <para id="para-00017">Compare your answer:</para>
    
    <para id="para-00018">No, because <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>14</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>64</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>16</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>56</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>16</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
  
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End --></section>
</content>
